{#
  The 404 page for the Symfony front controller, rendered by App\Http\LegacyBridge when the
  laminas application it bridges answers a request neither router knows with an HTML 404.

  It reproduces module/Application/view/error/404.phtml as production renders it — which is
  the two lines below and nothing else, because `display_exceptions` is off there, so the
  reason/controller/exception branches of that .phtml never draw. The heading and the
  "Page not found." message are `translate()`d exactly as the .phtml is, so the phrase rows
  already exist and both front controllers say the same thing.

  Why this exists rather than letting the bridge keep rendering the .phtml: Phase A of the
  laminas-mvc removal (2026-09-08). Once this is in place the bridge renders **no HTML page
  to any visitor** — after the canary was retired (Phase B, 2026-09-08) the bridge serves
  only the handful of unported laminas routes, all of which 404. See docs/strangler.md.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('A 404 error occurred') }}</h1>
<h2>{{ translate('Page not found.') }}</h2>
{% endblock %}
